  <article class="article-body">
    <div class="article-header">
      <h1>Spotify Song Suggester</h1>
      <p class="article-subtitle">
        Using a nearest-neighbors model to suggest the best music for anyone
      </p>
      <p class="article-date">
        <time datetime="2022-03-17">March 17, 2022</time>
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      <a
        href="https://spotify.com/"
        rel="external noopener"
        aria-label="Spotify (opens in new tab)">Spotify</a
      > is one of the most popular music streaming services in the world. For one
      of my most interesting projects yet, I was tasked with writing and training
      a machine learning model to suggest songs to a Spotify user based on their
      liked songs.
    </p>

    <p>
      Using a dataset of over half a million songs, I built a nearest-neighbors
      model with
      <a
        href="https://scikit-learn.org/stable/"
        rel="external noopener"
        aria-label="scikit-learn (opens in new tab)">scikit-learn</a
      > to generate 10 recommended songs from the dataset which most closely matched
      the attributes of the input songs. This model is an unsupervised classification
      problem, meaning the model has no "target variable" to learn from.
    </p>

    <p>
      The code for this project lives in the
      <a
        href="https://github.com/jacob-torres/Spotify-Song-Suggester"
        rel="external noopener"
        aria-label="Spotify Song Suggester repository on GitHub (opens in new tab)"
        >Spotify Song Suggester repository</a
      >, and the full Jupyter notebook is
      <a href="/notebooks/spotify-nearest-neighbors-model.html">available here</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Tools</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Python 3.8</li>
      <li>pandas and NumPy</li>
      <li>scikit-learn: StandardScaler, PCA, NearestNeighbors</li>
    </ul>

